00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:56.870
They think he's great.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:01.180
Is there some connection between that and
whatever kept McCarthy publicly supporting

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.180
Trump?

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.800
Could it be as simple as polling, they say?

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.900
Listen, most of the base supports this guy,
so we've got to support this guy.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:16.329
All of this confirms McCarthy is saying enough
to know about the toxicity and the atrocity

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:21.059
of Trump, and yet he still actively chose
to allow it.

00:04:21.059 --> 00:04:25.020
And that makes him, I believe, worse than
if he was a true believer in this kind of

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.849
gets back to the conversation we've been having
for a week or two now about what's worse,

00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:30.770
the true believers or the false believers.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:35.550
The 25th Amendment was exactly for situations
like these where the president has become

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:40.869
so compromised, he can't think straight, he
can't discharge his duty as president of the

00:04:40.869 --> 00:04:42.180
United States.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:47.949
He's lost his mind and some of the people
closest to him, I guess they knew it had been

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:50.699
enough, but they chose not to act.

00:04:50.699 --> 00:04:55.419
And they continue, Republicans do, to tell
Democrats now that they've got to clean up

00:04:55.419 --> 00:04:58.749
